            <ArticleTitle>[Diagnosis and management of food allergy in the rural environment].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>9-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Food allergy presents in two distinct forms: acute allergy with symptoms of anaphylactic type (acute urticaria, Quincke's oedema, anaphylactic shock); chronic allergy with symptoms of atopy (atopic dermatitis, asthma, rhinitis). Care in a rural environment includes the feature of distancing the care structure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
